<%# locals: (title:, level: :h2, row_class: "-mx-4 px-4") %>
<%# THE SECTION HEADER: a section's title that sticks under the rest of the pinned stack
    until the next section's header takes its place (docs/PAGE_HEADER.md).

    RENDER IT AS THE FIRST DIRECT CHILD OF ITS <section>. A sticky element travels only
    inside its parent, and that is what gives the swap: inside a wrapper div, it would
    leave with the wrapper. No backdrop-filter, transform or overflow on an ancestor.

      title      the heading's text.
      level      the heading's tag. A page should stick one level only: one bar at a time.
      row_class  the bleed. The default fits a container with px-4, as the page row's does.

    AT REST a normal title. STUCK it takes the bar. Its box never changes between the two.

    IT JOINS THE STACK WITH data-pin-section, NOT data-pin. Every header on the page shares
    one layer, `section`, and only the stuck one counts (studio/pinned_stack, stuckSection).
    So it positions off --pin-section-top, which also stands when none is stuck. Anything
    under the stack, such as a table's sticky header, sits under it with no edit. %>
<%= tag.div(class: "section-header #{row_class}".strip,
      style: "top: var(--pin-section-top, var(--nav-bottom, var(--nav-h, 0px))); z-index: calc(var(--z-sticky, 30) - 1)",
      data: { pin_section: "" }) do %>
  <%= content_tag(level, title, class: "section-header-title") %>
<% end %>
